 itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:18:41-07:00","id":1133184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1133001#post1133001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter 2e is already in Redlines and Mummy 2e hasn't yet made an appearance on the Monday Blog posts. Unless there was a lot of quiet behind the scenes work being done like with Geist 2e, Mummy 2e will probably come out right after Hunter 2e, possibly before Deviant as Mummy has a groundwork based in 1e while Deviant is being created from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a reasonable conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:43:07-07:00","id":1133351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1130736#post1130736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CtL2's KS is still slated for 2017. The brochure was put together and printed before we were sure the text would be finished in time to hit this year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thank goodness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T07:09:46-07:00","id":1134454,"title":"","content":"So i am curious about this KS, would we have a draft to check out before pledging? <br /> <br /> I ask because i wouldn't put money for David Hill\u00b4s version of changeling but i am not sure what elements are present in the new version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T07:32:30-07:00","id":1134460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134454#post1134454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am curious about this KS, would we have a draft to check out before pledging?<br /> <br /> I ask because i wouldn't put money for David Hill\u00b4s version of changeling but i am not sure what elements are present in the new version.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I seem to recall when Demon the Descent was on kickstarter, there was a draft of the text available on that kickstarter's main page. It's possible Changeling the Lost 2E could do the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T09:11:44-07:00","id":1134487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134460#post1134460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall when Demon the Descent was on kickstarter, there was a draft of the text available on that kickstarter's main page. It's possible Changeling the Lost 2E could do the same</div> </div> </div> </div>They did it with Beast's Kickstarter too, which is what lead to some of the last-minute changes to that game.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping they do the same for Changeling because my decision about whether or not to put money towards it also depends on how much of David's work makes it in. Just, in the other direction. If they scrapped the beautifully executed Seeming Blessing, Curse, Clarity, and Acuity system, I have no interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T09:15:51-07:00","id":1134489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134487#post1134487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did it with Beast's Kickstarter too, which is what lead to some of the last-minute changes to that game.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping they do the same for Changeling because my decision about whether or not to put money towards it also depends on how much of David's work makes it in. Just, in the other direction. If they scrapped the beautifully executed Seeming Blessing, Curse, Clarity, and Acuity system, I have no interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur with the integration of Seeming Blessing/Curse and Clarity, though I do prefer the more open source of Seeming now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:05:22-07:00","id":1134544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134487#post1134487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they scrapped the beautifully executed Seeming Blessing, Curse, Clarity, and Acuity system, I have no interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am on the other direction, hated his &quot;your seeming determines how you escape and is always THIS options&quot; and their seeming curses are something i dislike it too.<br /> <br /> I dont remember what acuity is, nor that Clarity was that different from 1E","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:09:22-07:00","id":1134546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134544#post1134544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am on the other direction, hated his &amp;quot;your seeming determines how you escape and is always THIS options&amp;quot; and their seeming curses are something i dislike it too.<br /> <br /> I dont remember what acuity is, nor that Clarity was that different from 1E</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarity was hugely different. You could only raise it through Clarity rolls instead of buying it. That was an awesome mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:14:27-07:00","id":1134550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134544#post1134544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont remember what acuity is, nor that Clarity was that different from 1E</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Underhill 2e Clarity was non-Experience-based and success or failure on a breaking point gave you a Condition that either boosted your Perception bonus with a risk of temporarily losing it and allowed you to raise your Clarity more than once per story (which lasted longer with higher Clarity) or made subsequent breaking points more likely to fail (which lasted longer with higher Wyrd). You got extra breaking points as your Wyrd went up and the breaking point pool was Attribute-based with the same pool as the rolls for Reaction to Surprise and generalized Perception.<br /> <br /> This was substantially different from 1e's more standardized model of Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:14:30-07:00","id":1134551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134489#post1134489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I concur with the integration of Seeming Blessing/Curse and Clarity, though I do prefer the more open source of Seeming now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am ok with making the narrative role of Seeming a little more flexible, but it's always a tradeoff between flexibility and specificity. Seeming-as-agency is in my opinion a much stronger metaphor than the new take, but also a narrower one. In my opinion, one of the greatest strengths of David's Changeling was its ludonarrative synchronicity. The mechanics and the prose were telling the same story. Now, if you weren't into the story they were both telling, I can understand why you'd be happier with the more open take on things. Personally though, I'll always prefer making a story stronger for those who enjoy it than making it weaker to appeal to more people. Same reason I think Promethean is better for not including optional transhumanist themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:27:37-07:00","id":1134558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134546#post1134546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity was hugely different. You could only raise it through Clarity rolls instead of buying it. That was an awesome mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134550#post1134550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Underhill 2e Clarity was non-Experience-based and success or failure on a breaking point gave you a Condition that either boosted your Perception bonus with a risk of temporarily losing it and allowed you to raise your Clarity more than once per story (which lasted longer with higher Clarity) or made subsequent breaking points more likely to fail (which lasted longer with higher Wyrd). You got extra breaking points as your Wyrd went up and the breaking point pool was Attribute-based with the same pool as the rolls for Reaction to Surprise and generalized Perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i really seems to be missremembering what i read on clarity. Seems nice on not penalizing the Player on having to waste XP to remain functional, whoever i have run into problems with the way the similar concept was put into Forsaken. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134551#post1134551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeming-as-agency is in my opinion a much stronger metaphor than the new take, but also a narrower one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can i ask you whats the new take? I am checking the blog notes but i am only finding hills version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134551#post1134551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally though, I'll always prefer making a story stronger for those who enjoy it than making it weaker to appeal to more people. Same reason I think Promethean is better for not including optional transhumanist themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am on the opposite boat here, i preffer a system that allows for alternatives takes on the game. I have found the best games on WoD have been those that had their intended themes replaced by the player base with better ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:28:02-07:00","id":1134559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134551#post1134551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am ok with making the narrative role of Seeming a little more flexible, but it's always a tradeoff between flexibility and specificity. Seeming-as-agency is in my opinion a much stronger metaphor than the new take, but also a narrower one. In my opinion, one of the greatest strengths of David's Changeling was its ludonarrative synchronicity. The mechanics and the prose were telling the same story. Now, if you weren't into the story they were both telling, I can understand why you'd be happier with the more open take on things. Personally though, I'll always prefer making a story stronger for those who enjoy it than making it weaker to appeal to more people. Same reason I think Promethean is better for not including optional transhumanist themes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For my preference, while I understood the direction Dave was taking for Seeming, I didn't particularly <i>like</i> it - namely, it would have been the first thing I'd house-rule out (creating a new axis of Role to represent what it was doing mechanically and narratively, without impacting other areas). With Seeming as it currently stands, it can represent the nature of Durance (1E), how you escaped/retook agency (Dave's), or how you chose to cope/define yourself after your escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:28:15-07:00","id":1134561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134544#post1134544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am on the other direction, hated his &quot;your seeming determines how you escape and is always THIS options&quot; and their seeming curses are something i dislike it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple things here. First of all, Seeming didn't determine how you escaped, how you escaped determined your Seeming. Second of all, &quot;It's always THIS option&quot; has always been a very shallow interpretation of the text. Lastly, you don't have to worry about that because they have changed the narrative role of Seemings from the Underhill version. I just hope they didn't throw the mechanically brilliant baby out with the too often misinterpreted bath water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134544#post1134544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont remember what acuity is, nor that Clarity was that different from 1E</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people have already covered this. The significant difference to me was that Clarity was both gained and lost by experiencing Breaking Points, and that Breaking Points were entirely personal. Seeming Blessings and Curses also tied into this, with the Blessing giving a way to get a guaranteed Clarity bump once per story by reinforcing your sense of agency, while Curse gave you an extra Breaking Point trigger. Acuity was the Condition you got on a Breaking Point success, and resolving it was the only way to regain Clarity outside of your Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> I also appreciated that Clarity Breaking Points were rolled with Wits + Composure instead of Resolve + Composure, but that was minor compared to the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-27-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:37:00-07:00","id":1134567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134561#post1134561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other people have already covered this. The significant difference to me was that Clarity was both gained and lost by experiencing Breaking Points, and that Breaking Points were entirely personal. Seeming Blessings and Curses also tied into this, with the Blessing giving a way to get a guaranteed Clarity bump once per story by reinforcing your sense of agency, while Curse gave you an extra Breaking Point trigger. Acuity was the Condition you got on a Breaking Point success, and resolving it was the only way to regain Clarity outside of your Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> I also appreciated that Clarity Breaking Points were rolled with Wits + Composure instead of Resolve + Composure, but that was minor compared to the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Blessing regained Clarity more of a <i>lack</i> of agency, as in it represented falling into stereotypes and burying your head in the sand? Whereas the Curse triggered Acuity represents actually confronting your trauma, and regaining a sense of self (Clarity) after seeing through it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:38:32-07:00","id":1134570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134558#post1134558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i ask you whats the new take? I am checking the blog notes but i am only finding hills version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose talked about it on the forums, basically it's kind of the nature of your Durance, but also kind of how you took agency, but also kind of how you define yourself after you escaped... it's all very wishy-washy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134558#post1134558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am on the opposite boat here, i preffer a system that allows for alternatives takes on the game. I have found the best games on WoD have been those that had their intended themes replaced by the player base with better ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your opinion and you're entitled to have it. Personally I agree with the adage, if you try to please everyone you end up pleasing no one. Case in point, there's nothing to dislike about this &quot;it represents whatever you want it to&quot; take on Seeming, but there's also nothing to like about it. It refuses to take any one stance for fear of alienating anyone who doesn't like that stance, and in exchange it gets a lukewarm reception from people who like all the stances it tries to dance between instead of a good reception from any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:45:50-07:00","id":1134577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134567#post1134567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the Blessing regained Clarity more of a <i>lack</i> of agency, as in it represented falling into stereotypes and burying your head in the sand?</div> </div> </div> </div>No? It was when you acted in a way that reflected your means of reclaiming agency, and in so doing, reinforcing that sense of agency in the same way you did back then. Flaunting social norms for Beasts, taking charge for Faerist, acting pragmatically for Darklings, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134567#post1134567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas the Curse triggered Acuity represents actually confronting your trauma, and regaining a sense of self (Clarity) after seeing through it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. A lot of people were reticent about Seeming Curses at first, because it seemed like getting a Breaking Point for confronting your trauma seemed to many to be punishing it, and therefore discouraging healthy means of coping. When Clarity was revealed though, it showed how facing your trauma is risky - it can be damaging - but also rewarding - it's the only way (apart from reinforcing the act that reclaimed your agency) to recover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:51:20-07:00","id":1134581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134570#post1134570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's your opinion and you're entitled to have it. Personally I agree with the adage, if you try to please everyone you end up pleasing no one. Case in point, there's nothing to dislike about this &quot;it represents whatever you want it to&quot; take on Seeming, but there's also nothing to like about it. It refuses to take any one stance for fear of alienating anyone who doesn't like that stance, and in exchange it gets a lukewarm reception from people who like all the stances it tries to dance between instead of a good reception from any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Rose version then, but on the example at hand. The way i see it, it allows the player who cares about seeming the freedom to make a character concept tie in some way to seeming (be for or <br /> Against) but also allows the Player/dm who doesnt care about seeming to ignore it and concentrate in other things.<br /> <br /> For example i had this NPC for a 1st edition game that i love: She was a Ogre/Oni lawyer whose durance was working in a bathhouse of onis. Saving tips/stealing until she was able to afford her freedom. Now she was a wannabe xanatos that was trapped in a Ogre body and temper. Now on Hills version that wouldnt fly as she had to escape through violence and thats that. One would say &quot;pick another seeming&quot; but in her case the seeming in conflict was the important of the character. This lawyer who wanted to be all dominating socially and constantly fails because she would flip her shit and violence was easier to her.<br /> <br /> Now on Rose/1st edition take seeming is &quot;meaningless unless i want it to be meaningful&quot;. It allows me to craft any story i want with seeming without any limitation but at the same time it allows me to ignore it if i dont feel it adds anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-27-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:54:46-07:00","id":1134583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134570#post1134570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose talked about it on the forums, basically it's kind of the nature of your Durance, but also kind of how you took agency, but also kind of how you define yourself after you escaped... it's all very wishy-washy.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's your opinion and you're entitled to have it. Personally I agree with the adage, if you try to please everyone you end up pleasing no one. Case in point, there's nothing to dislike about this &quot;it represents whatever you want it to&quot; take on Seeming, but there's also nothing to like about it. It refuses to take any one stance for fear of alienating anyone who doesn't like that stance, and in exchange it gets a lukewarm reception from people who like all the stances it tries to dance between instead of a good reception from any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd instead contest that 2E instead represents that Seeming isn't so simple as &quot;how you took agency&quot;, but can also come from how you define yourself, or how your Keeper defined you. It opens options without closing off anything narratively, should a ST or player wish it. It also means you can't just look at a Darkling and tell they betrayed someone to get here, or that a Fairest led/manipulated others to escape. It makes leaping to conclusions about a Changeling are problem <i>because</i> there is no hard rule about it.<br /> <br /> If you want Seeming determine by the nature of how a Changeling escaped, you can go right ahead and do so. If someone else wants to determine it by how their character reinvent themselves, they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:06:54-07:00","id":1134600,"title":"","content":"David's Changeling was everything I wanted out of a new edition of Changeling; mechanics that zeroed in on the beautiful themes of the first. Even barring my current situation regarding this company, I can't see myself being too hungry for a book that's even a little bit off what looked like a basically perfect swing at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:40:10-07:00","id":1134640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134454#post1134454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am curious about this KS, would we have a draft to check out before pledging?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the answer is yes, there will be.<br /> <br /> Rose had a manuscript of the CtL2e text on hand at GenCon 2017. Given past CofD corebook KS, it would be strange if it wasn't up with the KS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134583#post1134583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd instead contest that 2E instead represents that Seeming isn't so simple as &quot;how you took agency&quot;, but can also come from how you define yourself, or how your Keeper defined you. It opens options without closing off anything narratively, should a ST or player wish it. It also means you can't just look at a Darkling and tell they betrayed someone to get here, or that a Fairest led/manipulated others to escape. It makes leaping to conclusions about a Changeling are problem <i>because</i> there is no hard rule about it.<br /> <br /> If you want Seeming determine by the nature of how a Changeling escaped, you can go right ahead and do so. If someone else wants to determine it by how their character reinvent themselves, they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally: isn't the whole idea behind Changeling about forging their own stories?<br /> <br /> That the True Fae pluck humans from their lives, forcibly inserts them in their realm to act out whatever stories they want. And that the changeling, by choosing to escape, is basically taking a stand and saying &quot;No! This is MY story, not yours!&quot; Either by taking what their Keeper made them and making it their own, or using what changed them to help them escape.<br /> <br /> If anything, wouldn't having one option just be detrimental to the themes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:53:54-07:00","id":1134645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134583#post1134583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd instead contest that 2E instead represents that Seeming isn't so simple as &quot;how you took agency&quot;, but can also come from how you define yourself, or how your Keeper defined you. It opens options without closing off anything narratively, should a ST or player wish it. It also means you can't just look at a Darkling and tell they betrayed someone to get here, or that a Fairest led/manipulated others to escape. It makes leaping to conclusions about a Changeling are problem <i>because</i> there is no hard rule about it.<br /> <br /> If you want Seeming determine by the nature of how a Changeling escaped, you can go right ahead and do so. If someone else wants to determine it by how their character reinvent themselves, they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except because it can represent anything, that means it isn't really a representation of anything. If x can be caused by a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, etc. all separately, it doesn't narratively represent any of those. When it's so open so that the player can have it decided by any factor of the character, it may as well have been decided randomly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:16:58-07:00","id":1134653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134640#post1134640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally: isn't the whole idea behind Changeling about forging their own stories?<br /> <br /> That the True Fae pluck humans from their lives, forcibly inserts them in their realm to act out whatever stories they want. And that the changeling, by choosing to escape, is basically taking a stand and saying &amp;quot;No! This is MY story, not yours!&amp;quot; Either by taking what their Keeper made them and making it their own, or using what changed them to help them escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, exactly. David's Seemings fit perfectly into that framework, representing <i>how</i> you said &quot;this is my story.&quot; With the new, more general version of Seeming, it doesn't represent that any more. It doesn't, from what I have read, represent anything. Most X and Y splats in second edition answer questions. &quot;What have I become?&quot; and &quot;What do I do now?&quot; in Vampire; &quot;What do you hunt?&quot; and &quot;How do you hunt it?&quot; in Werewolf. In Underhill Changeling, it was going to be &quot;How did your Keeper change you?&quot; and &quot;How did you change yourself?&quot; What question do Kith and Seeming (or Seeming and Court, if you like) answer now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134640#post1134640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, wouldn't having one option just be detrimental to the themes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would. Fortunately, David's version has never only given you one option. Knowing someone isn't a Darkling doesn't tell you they betrayed someone to escape, all it tells you is that they had the choice between doing the altruistic thing or escaping, and they chose to escape. The forms that making that decision takes are as varied as the people who made them, the betrayal thing was just an example. Granted, maybe the examples were too easy to misinterpret as the only possible expressions of the Seemings, and maybe David should have pushed for more extensive rewrites to make this clear. But the fact of the matter is, the Underhill take on Seemings wasn't nearly as restrictive as it's often made out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:04:00-07:00","id":1134664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134645#post1134645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except because it can represent anything, that means it isn't really a representation of anything. If x can be caused by a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, etc. all separately, it doesn't narratively represent any of those. When it's so open so that the player can have it decided by any factor of the character, it may as well have been decided randomly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except, it isn't decided but just &quot;anything&quot;? It is all related to a character and their Durance: During, Breaking Out, or After. It isn't, &quot;oh, my character saw a bird some day - therefore, Beast&quot;. It <i>has</i> meaning - it just isn't forced into only being one event that could determine it. You can have Fairest who didn't become leaders to escape. Beasts who betrayed someone else to do so. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134653#post1134653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would. Fortunately, David's version has never only given you one option. Knowing someone isn't a Darkling doesn't tell you they betrayed someone to escape, all it tells you is that they had the choice between doing the altruistic thing or escaping, and they chose to escape. The forms that making that decision takes are as varied as the people who made them, the betrayal thing was just an example. Granted, maybe the examples were too easy to misinterpret as the only possible expressions of the Seemings, and maybe David should have pushed for more extensive rewrites to make this clear. But the fact of the matter is, the Underhill take on Seemings wasn't nearly as restrictive as it's often made out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something seems to have been lost in the delivery, then. Because on reading, it strongly looks like that's the way your earn your <s>wings</s>Seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134653#post1134653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, exactly. David's Seemings fit perfectly into that framework, representing <i>how</i> you said &quot;this is my story.&quot; With the new, more general version of Seeming, it doesn't represent that any more. It doesn't, from what I have read, represent anything. Most X and Y splats in second edition answer questions. &quot;What have I become?&quot; and &quot;What do I do now?&quot; in Vampire; &quot;What do you hunt?&quot; and &quot;How do you hunt it?&quot; in Werewolf. In Underhill Changeling, it was going to be &quot;How did your Keeper change you?&quot; and &quot;How did you change yourself?&quot; What question do Kith and Seeming (or Seeming and Court, if you like) answer now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeming: What type of fae are you? Now, this could be determined by how your gave your Keeper the Finger. Or it could be how your choose to embrace your Freedom. Or maybe it was chosen for your during your Durance, and now you must live with it.<br /> <br /> Addendum: I've always (and still) see Kiths as more &quot;chrome&quot; you use to embellish your character to embody the vast diversity of fairy tale beings without having 101 Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-27-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:06:23-07:00","id":1134665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134653#post1134653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, exactly. David's Seemings fit perfectly into that framework, representing <i>how</i> you said &quot;this is my story.&quot; With the new, more general version of Seeming, it doesn't represent that any more. It doesn't, from what I have read, represent anything. Most X and Y splats in second edition answer questions. &quot;What have I become?&quot; and &quot;What do I do now?&quot; in Vampire; &quot;What do you hunt?&quot; and &quot;How do you hunt it?&quot; in Werewolf. In Underhill Changeling, it was going to be &quot;How did your Keeper change you?&quot; and &quot;How did you change yourself?&quot; What question do Kith and Seeming (or Seeming and Court, if you like) answer now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it wouldnt be &quot;your story&quot; but instead David Hills narrow version of it.<br /> <br /> As for question i would say seeming/kith answer the question of what your durance made you. Or for those that dont care about it, it can just be &quot; what you are&quot;<br /> <br /> And it can range from service ogre or fighter legolas-like elf. Concepts that were out of hills version. Which btw is kinda baffling that in both hills version and 1st edition there wasnt a easy way to play a legolas elf warrior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-27-2017, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:25:16-07:00","id":1134670,"title":"","content":"Without having read what the current Second Edition is like on the second, one of the big strengths of the Underhill version was that it was very much character first as far as Seemings were concerned. Sure, it had to constrain itself to archetypes, much as you have to in a game format, but those expectations were &quot;what a person would do&quot; rather than &quot;what does Faerie see me as&quot;, which is an argument that can be levied at our (admittedly limited) view at Second Edition's current iteration of Seemings, which is...I don't want to say less-clear, but I will say more-amalgamate than the Underhill version.<br /> <br /> Mind you, we haven't seen current Seemings as intended, beyond dev explanation. We might be shooting at shadows here.<br /> <br /> Also mind you, fanbases are more image focused than meaning focused. That's not a criticism, per se, but it is true-players just want to make their characters as exact as they can, within their own sense of purview before all else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:41:51-07:00","id":1134678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134665#post1134665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it wouldnt be &quot;your story&quot; but instead David Hills narrow version of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, you're mixing metaphors here. The meta-narrative of taking control of your own story from captors who tried to make it theirs occurs in-universe. David Hill does not exist in-universe, he's a real person. And he wrote the meta-narrative in question. Second of all, it's not nearly as narrow as you keep making it out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134665#post1134665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for question i would say seeming/kith answer the question of what your durance made you. Or for those that dont care about it, it can just be &quot; what you are&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134665#post1134665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it can range from service ogre or fighter legolas-like elf. Concepts that were out of hills version. Which btw is kinda baffling that in both hills version and 1st edition there wasnt a easy way to play a legolas elf warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of those concepts are entirely possible within the Underhill Kith/Seeming framework. They're a little shallow as concepts and you might have to flesh out a bit more of their stories, but you wouldn't have to scrap those aspects of the characters to make them work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:12:14-07:00","id":1134692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134678#post1134678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, you're mixing metaphors here. The meta-narrative of taking control of your own story from captors who tried to make it theirs occurs in-universe. David Hill does not exist in-universe, he's a real person. And he wrote the meta-narrative in question. Second of all, it's not nearly as narrow as you keep making it out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it was, all ogre/fairest/etc escaped the same way because of hills narrow vision of what seeming was. All fairest escape through leadership even though not all fairest pc concept follow the social route. Same with ogres and wizened etc.<br /> <br /> Is like saying &quot;behold! Changeling the game to represent any kind of fairy tale/myth you want during your durance.......as long as fairest lead, ogres use violence, etc. Oh you got an idea of a seeming that escape through other methods? Sorry go back to play 1st&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134678#post1134678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of those concepts are entirely possible within the Underhill Kith/Seeming framework. They're a little shallow as concepts and you might have to flesh out a bit more of their stories, but you wouldn't have to scrap those aspects of the characters to make them work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already posted the reclutant ogre and how she wasnt compatible with hills vision<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134581#post1134581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example i had this NPC for a 1st edition game that i love: She was a Ogre/Oni lawyer whose durance was working in a bathhouse of onis. Saving tips/stealing until she was able to afford her freedom. Now she was a wannabe xanatos that was trapped in a Ogre body and temper. Now on Hills version that wouldnt fly as she had to escape through violence and thats that. One would say &quot;pick another seeming&quot; but in her case the seeming in conflict was the important of the character. This lawyer who wanted to be all dominating socially and constantly fails because she would flip her shit and violence was easier to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could say &quot;she could have escaped through violence and then decided to try not to use it ever again&quot; or &quot;make her a wizened&quot; but then i would be forced to acomodate the character to hills rules instead of hills rules helping me make a better story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-27-2017, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T19:23:09-07:00","id":1134712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134653#post1134653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, exactly. David's Seemings fit perfectly into that framework, representing <i>how</i> you said &quot;this is my story.&quot; With the new, more general version of Seeming, it doesn't represent that any more. It doesn't, from what I have read, represent anything. Most X and Y splats in second edition answer questions. &quot;What have I become?&quot; and &quot;What do I do now?&quot; in Vampire; &quot;What do you hunt?&quot; and &quot;How do you hunt it?&quot; in Werewolf. In Underhill Changeling, it was going to be &quot;How did your Keeper change you?&quot; and &quot;How did you change yourself?&quot; What question do Kith and Seeming (or Seeming and Court, if you like) answer now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question answered by Kith is &quot;What did your Keeper make you into?&quot;, and Seeming is &quot;What have you become?&quot; Seeming to me seems like a changeling's perception of themselves. It is what they see when they look in the mirror, beyond simply their Kith.<br /> <br /> Those who identify strongly with the horrible experience they went through have the Seeming that matches what their Keeper desired. They are defining themselves according to their trauma. Basically, they are saying, &quot;This is who I am now. Look at me! This is what They did to me!&quot; An Ogre dwells on the constant abuse they suffered. A Beast laments their loss of humanity as they were forced to act as an animal. Changelings with Seemings gained from their Durance are dwelling in the past, unable and perhaps unwilling to let go of those defining traumas. No matter how far they run or what they do, they will always see themselves as victims of the Others.<br /> <br /> Others focus on the moment at which they changed things, taking their freedom into their own hands. They define themselves according to that moment. They are saying, &quot;This is who I am now. One decision made all the difference, and now my life is my own.&quot; An Ogre recounts the day they stopped working and decided to fight their way out. A Darkling can't get over the moment that they left their friend behind. For good or ill, these changelings dwell on a past moment as well, but in their case, it could be as simple as one choice that has marked them forever. It was still their choice, however, and that is an important distinction.<br /> <br /> Then there's the ones that focus on what they're doing now. They are saying, &quot;This is who I am now. I will do things my way, so that I never end up like that again.&quot; An Ogre lashes out at anyone around them, either out of a love for the fight or fear of anyone growing too close. A Darkling clings to the shadows, finding comfort in the disturbing reputation they've built. These changelings are basing their identity on choice as well, but in this case, it is an ongoing mode of action rather than a potential one time decision. It is easy to say that they are looking to the future rather than dwelling on the past, but that's not entirely fair. Their actions might very well be based on past trauma, but they still focus on how they're going to function from now on.<br /> <br /> The Underhill version of Seemings was interesting, don't get me wrong. It was still limited, however. My wife hated it, because she felt like it forced her into a certain type of backstory. It kind of did, too. If you wanted to play an Ogre character, you had to fight your way out in some way. You couldn't play one that had an ogre-like Keeper that made all its changelings into flesh-eating ogres, and one night snuck out while everyone was sleeping, leaving its brother behind. That character would more likely end up a Darkling in the Underhill version. At the very least, you'd need to have the character kill a guard on the way out to keep them an Ogre. Instead of having an Ogre that escapes the day it says, &quot;Okay, I'm done with violence,&quot; it needs to say, &quot;Okay, this is the last one.&quot; It also closes off the door to a Seeming for a changeling who was neglected or abandoned by their Keeper. About the only way to have multiple options of Seeming for a given backstory would be if the changeling's escape fulfilled multiple criteria. A warrior who called the others together and led a bloody rampage out of the doors to Arcadia could be a Fairest or an Ogre, but probably not an Elemental or Darkling. <br /> <br /> TLDR: The Underhill version of Seeming asked &quot;How did one moment forever define what you would be?&quot; while the new version seems to ask &quot;How are you defined?&quot; While it is still possible to make it about a single moment, it also opens up options for defining oneself based upon the trauma one has suffered or the method one is using to cope with that on an ongoing basis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T20:00:05-07:00","id":1134721,"title":"","content":"the underhill version of 2nd edition drifted so far away from the original edition of changeling (mechanically) that it was hardly recognizable as the same game. this was a problem for me, as it is rather difficult to get everyone in my gaming group to spend the time to memorize a whole drastically new rule set when they have just attained mastery with the old system. i'm also a big fan of subtlety, and i found that the underhill take on the game was way to obvs with the its take on the changelings being allegorical fantasy abuse survivors. i was totally going to sit this one out, as i already have all of 1e Lost but everything i have seen from the rose revision, including the uncoupling of definitive Seeming/Agency angle, is luring me back. <br /> <br /> i do hope that 2e includes elements of underhill's freehold system tho. i really thought that was lovely!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T20:37:18-07:00","id":1134731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134692#post1134692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it was, all ogre/fairest/etc escaped the same way because of hills narrow vision of what seeming was. All fairest escape through leadership even though not all fairest pc concept follow the social route. Same with ogres and wizened etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is a shallow reading. All fairest escape through <i>taking charge</i>, not necessarily through leadership, though leadership is a good example of one way this might be expressed. All Ogres escaped through violence, yes. All Wizened escaped through mastery of... something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134692#post1134692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is like saying &quot;behold! Changeling the game to represent any kind of fairy tale/myth you want during your durance.......as long as fairest lead, ogres use violence, etc. Oh you got an idea of a seeming that escape through other methods? Sorry go back to play 1st&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Changeling has ever been sold as the game to represent any kind of fairy tale/myth you want, durance or otherwise. It has always been the game about examining the story of abuse victims through the lens of fairy tales. The Seemings in Hill's version were also broad enough to cover almost any Durance and means of escape you can think of in <i>some</i> way. If none of them were a perfect fit, it's a toolbox game. You can always come up with a custom Blessing and Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134692#post1134692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already posted the reclutant ogre and how she wasnt compatible with hills vision<br /> <br /> One could say &quot;she could have escaped through violence and then decided to try not to use it ever again&quot; or &quot;make her a wizened&quot; but then i would be forced to acomodate the character to hills rules instead of hills rules helping me make a better story.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing about her story that couldn't work in the Underhill version. She probably wouldn't be a great fit for an Ogre without changing a few details of her backstory, I can't help but feel like complaining that your character who escaped by buying her freedom can't be an Ogre is a bit like complaining that your Promethean character who was stitched together from disparate body parts and animated with lightning can't be an Ulgan. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134712#post1134712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underhill version of Seemings was interesting, don't get me wrong. It was still limited, however. My wife hated it, because she felt like it forced her into a certain type of backstory. It kind of did, too. If you wanted to play an Ogre character, you had to fight your way out in some way. You couldn't play one that had an ogre-like Keeper that made all its changelings into flesh-eating ogres, and one night snuck out while everyone was sleeping, leaving its brother behind. That character would more likely end up a Darkling in the Underhill version. At the very least, you'd need to have the character kill a guard on the way out to keep them an Ogre. Instead of having an Ogre that escapes the day it says, &quot;Okay, I'm done with violence,&quot; it needs to say, &quot;Okay, this is the last one.&quot; It also closes off the door to a Seeming for a changeling who was neglected or abandoned by their Keeper. About the only way to have multiple options of Seeming for a given backstory would be if the changeling's escape fulfilled multiple criteria. A warrior who called the others together and led a bloody rampage out of the doors to Arcadia could be a Fairest or an Ogre, but probably not an Elemental or Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you wanted to play a character who didn't fight their way out, why would you want to play an Ogre? Literally the only thing being an Ogre did for you was gave you free Clarity for using violence, and a Breaking Point trigger for being confronted with the fact that you're in pain. Why would you even want that if your character snuck away and left their brother behind? Because their Keeper made them a flesh-eating ogre? That's Kith in Underhill. Play a Bloodbrute. Or make a custom Kith for it if none of the sample ones are a good fit for what you have in mind. Or modify an existing one if you like it's Blessing but don't like it's fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134712#post1134712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TLDR: The Underhill version of Seeming asked &quot;How did one moment forever define what you would be?&quot; while the new version seems to ask &quot;How are you defined?&quot; While it is still possible to make it about a single moment, it also opens up options for defining oneself based upon the trauma one has suffered or the method one is using to cope with that on an ongoing basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what to say, other than that I <u><i><b>emphaticallly</b></i></u> disagree with that interpretation of Underhill Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T21:06:25-07:00","id":1134740,"title":"","content":"It is a real shame that the massive thread derailment is allowed and why it is being allowed is even worse.<br /> <br /> As to the last thread relevant point, I don't know if they will release the text. Why should they? People unhappy with changes won't buy. They made their minds up already. People happy the game shifted back more to what the original changeling game was that so many enjoyed shouldn't need to see it. It might encourage them to spend a little more, so there is that.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't they? Well, who wants this bullshit to continue the whole time during the kickstarter? Probably not Onyx Path. I imagine the most significant reason would be if they keep doing it then people will expect it more than they already do. It may not make sense to have more corebook KS and release the full text. Maybe White Wolf doesn't see it as a good idea. Perhaps, they want to see how it goes without a release.<br /> <br /> There may be more reasons not to release than to release, so I'm not expected it. Everyone should be grateful to see a chapter or two. Some won't, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T21:26:30-07:00","id":1134749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134740#post1134740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a real shame that the massive thread derailment is allowed and why it is being allowed is even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>We generally allow a certain amount of topic drift, and in this case someone basically said &quot;I'm not buying if it's too much like David's version&quot;, and I don't think it's at all unreasonable to allow folks to voice the opposite opinion, or to allow either to discuss reasons for those purchasing decisions. That said, we are getting pretty far from the topic at this point, and I think we're to the point where nothing constructive is being said any more. It's probably time to drop this sidetrack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134740#post1134740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the last thread relevant point, I don't know if they will release the text. Why should they? People unhappy with changes won't buy. They made their minds up already. People happy the game shifted back more to what the original changeling game was that so many enjoyed shouldn't need to see it. It might encourage them to spend a little more, so there is that.<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't they? Well, who wants this bullshit to continue the whole time during the kickstarter? Probably not Onyx Path. I imagine the most significant reason would be if they keep doing it then people will expect it more than they already do. It may not make sense to have more corebook KS and release the full text. Maybe White Wolf doesn't see it as a good idea. Perhaps, they want to see how it goes without a release.<br /> <br /> There may be more reasons not to release than to release, so I'm not expected it. Everyone should be grateful to see a chapter or two. Some won't, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug*. So far, they've revealed the complete text of the book in all of the kickstarters, so there's no reason to assume that trend won't continue. Especially since they brought the complete text of Changeling to Gen Con to show at the booth. Unfortunately, it seems like anyone who frequents these forums who may have gone to Gen Con either didn't read it, or doesn't feel like sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T22:11:11-07:00","id":1134755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134749#post1134749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug*. So far, they've revealed the complete text of the book in all of the kickstarters, so there's no reason to assume that trend won't continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly they didn't do that in the latest kickstarter (though that's a result of the book not being written yet), so that might be the cause of doubt in some peoples minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T22:13:28-07:00","id":1134756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134755#post1134755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Admittedly they didn't do that in the latest kickstarter (though that's a result of the book not being written yet), so that might be the cause of doubt in some peoples minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Rich pretty explicitly said in the GenCon panel that having the text ready before the Kickstarter is an absolute must for OPP, unless it is Dark Eras. So I'm certain we will see exactly what we are getting in October.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T22:45:40-07:00","id":1134758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134740#post1134740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should they? People unhappy with changes won't buy. They made their minds up already. People happy the game shifted back more to what the original changeling game was that so many enjoyed shouldn't need to see it. It might encourage them to spend a little more, so there is that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe showing the people what those changes or aren't would give them some fucking confidence. Right now the situation is &quot;there was something good, that's gone now, and we don't know what's replacing it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T23:02:04-07:00","id":1134759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134756#post1134756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Rich pretty explicitly said in the GenCon panel that having the text ready before the Kickstarter is an absolute must for OPP, unless it is Dark Eras. So I'm certain we will see exactly what we are getting in October.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not all of them. Like, for the WoD20 books, that seems to be a lot looser.<br /> <br /> None of the WoD20 core books had their text completely ready when their KSs went up. And while W20 Shattered Dream's had the text ready, conversely V20 Beckett's Jyhad Diary did not.<br /> <br /> CofD core books, yeah I can see a stronger case for having the text ready. Especially if the intent past CtL2 is to give the remaining CofD books that don't have 2nd editions their own KSs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T07:26:33-07:00","id":1134826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134740#post1134740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why shouldn't they? Well, who wants this bullshit to continue the whole time during the kickstarter? Probably not Onyx Path. I imagine the most significant reason would be if they keep doing it then people will expect it more than they already do. It may not make sense to have more corebook KS and release the full text. Maybe White Wolf doesn't see it as a good idea. Perhaps, they want to see how it goes without a release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because as of right now we dont know all the changes. So its kinda the worst of both worlds.<br /> <br /> People like atamajakki and Charlaquin are on the camp:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134758#post1134758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;there was something good, that's gone now, and we don't know what's replacing it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While people like me is on the camp of &quot;There was something awful, it is gone now? How much is gone?&quot; Both of camps are reluctant to put money on it unless we know the form the product is gonna take.<br /> <br /> I remember reading the author of beast saying that showing the draft was a bad idea, and they also didnt do it for M20 if i remember right. But i hope they do so i know whether to put money on it or avoid it and dont waste my money like with M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-28-2017, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:58:15-07:00","id":1134860,"title":"","content":"Not to continue the thread derail, but I think this is relevant in the sense of talking about what has changed post-Underhill:<br /> <br /> A) In the Underhill version at least, you couldn't look at someone and tell what Seeming they were. That was explicitly stated. You looked at a changeling and saw a large brutish giant with fangs.<br /> <br /> B) In the Underhill version (and I'm thinking this will still be around in a slightly different form) Ogre Seeming =/= large brutish giant with fangs, it equaled 'someone who used violence to escape' (The new version seems to be 'someone who was turned into a violent thing, someone who uses violence now that they have escaped, or someone who used violence to escape').<br /> <br /> Between these two points, the idea that you can't play an 'Ogre' that isn't violent is flawed because an Ogre Seeming is a game mechanics concept and not an in universe one. You can be a Concept!ogre without being a Seeming!Ogre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Slight grammatical correction. 08-28-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:19:49-07:00","id":1134916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134826#post1134826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because as of right now we dont know all the changes. So its kinda the worst of both worlds.<br /> <br /> People like atamajakki and Charlaquin are on the camp:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While people like me is on the camp of &amp;quot;There was something awful, it is gone now? How much is gone?&amp;quot; Both of camps are reluctant to put money on it unless we know the form the product is gonna take.<br /> <br /> I remember reading the author of beast saying that showing the draft was a bad idea, and they also didnt do it for M20 if i remember right. But i hope they do so i know whether to put money on it or avoid it and dont waste my money like with M20.</div> </div> </div> </div> That there is this much of a divide is bad for Changeling. <br /> <br /> I hope that Rose can find a compromise everyone (or at most) can find, acceptable. <br /> <br /> For my part I've decided to just treat David Hill's Version as a semiofficial supplement to the Changeling 2e Core that I can poach from as I wish, effectively combining them. <br /> <br /> Feel free to do the same if it will help. That way even if you prefer say David's approach to Seemings fluff and their interactions with Clarity, but say prefer Rose/Meghans's Regalia, Contracts, and Goblin Queen Condition, you can do that so it will still be worth donating to get the Changeling 2e Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T23:07:29-07:00","id":1135077,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> here - you still got all the material David shared in previous months. Myself, I will <i>incorporate</i> David's version into Rose's one - like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1134783-rose-s-2e-seemings-as-narrative-turning-point\">I proposed in this topic</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1134783-seemings-as-narrative-turning-point#post1134783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last few days I have wondered on interesting ( I hope ) theory on this idea - <b>That (final) 2E Seeming are Narrative Turning Point for changelings lives. </b> If most important event to character was her way to free herself from Keeper - then in that instance Seeming is established for her. If it was Keeper laying 'curse' on changeling ( like Enchantress changing Prince into Beast in <b>'Beauty and the Beast'</b> ), then Seeming for changeling is set then. And if characters return to Earth without Seeming till then, it's determined how she was coping with hazards of Hedge on her way back - as her journey from Hedge to Earth was most important event.<br /> <br /> Just theory, but sounds as it works with spoiled information.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1134783-seemings-as-narrative-turning-point?p=1134803#post1134803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that like 1/3 of all 2E changelings have CHOSEN their Seeming by defying their Keeper and - literally - <i>choosing their story </i> - like Fairest leading small revolt in Arcadia. Then second 1/3 are those that Keeper 'cursed' or modeled to be their Seemings - like 'immoral Fairest', made to be vain by Keeper, like his Gentry 'little princess'. And the rest of 1/3 are those that 'simply run away', when Keeper was not looking - they can be Seemingless if they not change their story till they come to the Earth. I think this is where most Grimms can come, as they are from times where Keepers en masse have more important problems ( change of Contracts and Pledges ) than looking for their servants. As changeling did not do something truly defining it's next story - he do not have Seeming chosen, yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I written when David's previews comes - his idea was very good for some part of 1E characters pool, dramatic good. But deleting rest of 1E character concepts for Seeming was not good for the gameline, as general. With making David's version part of great group of each Seemings stories in Rose's version, we have best of two worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-29-2017, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T00:03:47-07:00","id":1135083,"title":"","content":"It's really not the best of both worlds. Yeah, the playtest stuff from David's version still exists, and we can borrow from that if we like. As I mentioned earlier though, one of the great strengths of David's version was it's ludonarrative synchronicity. Grafting David's fluff onto different mechanics wouldn't be nearly as poignant because the mechanics and the fluff in David's version were so tightly linked, each enhancing the other. Likewise, David's mechanics wouldn't fit as well with different fluff. And trying to merge his game with Rose's only serves to water both down. I'd much rather Rose's version be the best it can be on its own than to weaken its own metaphors by trying to incorporate the possibility of David's metaphors. I'd rather the game make <i>strong choices</i> than waffle between &quot;well, it's kinda this, but also kinda that, and under certain conditions, maybe it's sorta like the other thing too.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:16:55-07:00","id":1135104,"title":"","content":"Limiting games fandom is not really making game stronger - it's only making it's more elitist. Do not throw your baby out of the bath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:35:21-07:00","id":1135107,"title":"","content":"My view is &quot;Other gamelines have their mechanics resonate with their themes and reinforce the metaphors of the game, even if doing so doesn't necessarily match everyone's preferred style of play. So why is there opposition for the same thing with Changeling?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T03:01:33-07:00","id":1135111,"title":"","content":"Because it's made on much less way than in David's 2E Seemings, and his version narrative enforcement. Let's look on other 2E X-Splats, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Clans</b> - beside nice fluff, most identity of them are only in Clan Bane, really - I can make 4 different Nosferatu vampires on the rules, not going against splat write-up in 2E corebook, it's so ambiguous. They<i> literally</i> give you three different origins stories of each Clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf Auspices</b> - It's only tells you 'what way you hunt' - just like Seeming tells you 'what way you are fae' in 1E. Adding Moon Phases is nice tie-in, but not really limiting character concepts - any one can be made to First Change on 'First Quarter of the Moon'.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage Paths</b> - Two Ruling Arcana and Supernal Beings you summon or see in Mage Sight. All that it is here, really. Added Tarot assosiation is nice fluff, but not really limiting players choices in character creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Linages</b> - The way you were Created plus your Humor. Maybe a bit more enforcing than rest, but it's only limited to how Demiurge or Genitor took bodies that made you. From then on it's totally your story. It's on the same par as Kith, I may add.<br /> <br /> <b>David's 2E Changeling Seemings</b> - All of them assume you won you freedom from Keeper cretin way - you needed to do things that define each David's Seemings, nothing other will grant you powers, Curse and Blessing of Seeming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It works great if you agree with David's Seeming vision - but it alienates anyone other not agreeing with his 'Seemings stories'. I like to play sometimes 'rebel leading Faeirest' - but also 'immoral princess', making her much more Gentry-like.<br /> <br /> I will be direct here - to point out that David's Seemings are extremely restricting the players' background in comparison to the other 2E games. That's why open definition of Rose's is really way to go with it - if you agree with David's vision, you totally still can have it. If you not - you all are still fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-29-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T09:37:12-07:00","id":1135182,"title":"","content":"They're not at all that restrictive, and the same way you can say &quot;all Clan gives you in Vampire is Clan Bane&quot;, the only thing David's Seemings gave you was Seeming Blessing and Curse. The stories were just examples. This was stated repeatedly by David in the forums, as well as at the beginning of the Seemings section. As long as the Seeming Blessing could be spun as a reflection of how your character escaped - flaunting social norms for Beasts, acting pragmatically for Darklings, acting erratically for Elementals, taking charge for Fairest, using violence for Ogres, or mastering something for Wizened, that character could fit that Seeming. They were broad enough that you could cover almost any means of escape with one of them. The problem is, everyone insisted on reading them as shallowly as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T10:26:23-07:00","id":1135197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135182#post1135182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the Seeming Blessing could be spun as a reflection of how your character escaped - flaunting social norms for Beasts, acting pragmatically for Darklings, acting erratically for Elementals, taking charge for Fairest, using violence for Ogres, or mastering something for Wizened, that character could fit that Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what some people disliked, being forced to make all ogres escape through violence, all fairest escape through taking charge etc etc. Is not doing a shallow reading when one reads that and say &quot;yeah that seems too limiting to me&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T10:36:47-07:00","id":1135201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135182#post1135182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not at all that restrictive, and the same way you can say &amp;quot;all Clan gives you in Vampire is Clan Bane&amp;quot;, the only thing David's Seemings gave you was Seeming Blessing and Curse. The stories were just examples. This was stated repeatedly by David in the forums, as well as at the beginning of the Seemings section. As long as the Seeming Blessing could be spun as a reflection of how your character escaped - flaunting social norms for Beasts, acting pragmatically for Darklings, acting erratically for Elementals, taking charge for Fairest, using violence for Ogres, or mastering something for Wizened, that character could fit that Seeming. They were broad enough that you could cover almost any means of escape with one of them. The problem is, everyone insisted on reading them as shallowly as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Seemings also influenced character appearance and future aspects of th Contracts that they'd learn. <br /> <br /> Which Seeming do you think would go best for one that just makes a desperate break for it and is lucky enough to not get caught? You're an Ogre if you punch a guy on the way or a Darkling if you leave someone behind, but what if you do neither? For that matter, could the sole changeling of a Keeper ever become a Fairest in an escape?<br /> <br /> My biggest problem (and my wife's, to an even greater degree) with that version was the fact that your Seeming came down to a single choice. Someone who lived a peaceful life, had a comparatively peaceful Durance, and tries to live a peaceful life afterwards is just as much an Ogre as someone who used violence for everything before, during, and after their Durance, provided that the first used violence that one time to escape. I'm not saying that having one decision forever shape a character is necessarily a bad thing (and I will still frequently make use of the option), but I like that the new version seems to place the greatest defining event into the players' hands rather than specifying what that defining event had to be. This change means that I can more easily convert characters from first edition to second without needing to decide between changing backstory or changing Seeming.<br /> <br /> I apologize if my post seems antagonistic. It isn't intended to, but replying on my phone makes it a bit of a pain to keep going back to refine it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T11:26:38-07:00","id":1135217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135201#post1135201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Seeming do you think would go best for one that just makes a desperate break for it and is lucky enough to not get caught?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underhill Seemings leaned on the narrative trends of ex-captives in 1e, those being that for the most part you either dramatically changed something about yourself to escape or you were let go, each of which fed into a different point of concern after your return to Earth. Something as significant to a changeling's story as their Durance doesn't end in a narratively compelling fashion with &quot;I just made a desperate break for it and got lucky&quot; when you're talking about escaping from a fortune-favored god-monster, at least not when looked at comprehensively.<br /> <br /> Changeling is one of the lines that least benefits from the shallow reading of Vampire's answer to &quot;how did you become this kind of monster?&quot; because the process is substantially more obviously gradual and involved on account of requiring physical transportation to another world. &quot;Second Edition's generally increased focus on how acquiring a template works and happens in-story means I can't as easily disregard backstory and treat my character as a normal human with magic powers thrown on&quot; is not ever going to be a compelling argument for looser standards of character creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For that matter, could the sole changeling of a Keeper ever become a Fairest in an escape? </div> </div> </div>Changelings and Fae have never been the entire population of Arcadia by a long shot. The Underhill Fairest got out by using others, whether those others were changelings, Strangers, hobgoblins, friendly birds, or what have you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone who lived a peaceful life, had a comparatively peaceful Durance, and tries to live a peaceful life afterwards is just as much an Ogre as someone who used violence for everything before, during, and after their Durance, provided that the first used violence that one time to escape. </div> </div> </div>&quot;That one time&quot; is a formative and character-defining moment regardless of whether it mechanically determines your seeming, because &quot;that one time&quot; led to you <i>becoming a different person</i>. It also <i>follows from the person that you used to be</i> most of the time.<br /> <br /> If your character had a peaceful life and a peaceful Durance, where does it follow that they should aesthetically be calloused and lacking in outward vulnerability? What part of their Durance and their personality led them to determine that hardening their heart and mien was the best way for them to escape? Where does the need for physical insensitivity and emotional fragility come into play for such a character?<br /> <br /> It's <i>technically possible </i>to make an Ogre whose background and Durance supplied no real explanation for their decision to escape through the story-beats of an Ogre's rebirth, but putting the onus on you to figure out how that works was not unique to the Underhill model of Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-29-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:00:50-07:00","id":1135228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135197#post1135197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what some people disliked, being forced to make all ogres escape through violence, all fairest escape through taking charge etc etc. Is not doing a shallow reading when one reads that and say &quot;yeah that seems too limiting to me&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Being an ogre was defined as having escaped through violence. I fail to see what is limiting about &quot;My character who escaped through non-violent means can't have escaped through violence.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135201#post1135201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Seemings also influenced character appearance and future aspects of th Contracts that they'd learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gave suggestions for what character appearance might look like, but it was also explicit that one cannot tell a Changeling's Seeming by their appearance. This is another case of taking what was meant to be examples as being absolutes, and then complaining the source material is too absolutist. As for Seeming Contract bonuses, any character could learn any of them for a measly 1 experience each. Your Seeming just gave you a few for free. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135201#post1135201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Seeming do you think would go best for one that just makes a desperate break for it and is lucky enough to not get caught? You're an Ogre if you punch a guy on the way or a Darkling if you leave someone behind, but what if you do neither? For that matter, could the sole changeling of a Keeper ever become a Fairest in an escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>With that as the backstory? Unseemly. &quot;I just got lucky&quot; isn't a seizing of agency. I could potentially see that backstory being fleshed out into something that could fit well as Beast or Elemental, but as-is, that character hasn't taken back their own story, so they don't have a Seeming. Yes, the sole changeling of a Keeper could become a Fairest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135201#post1135201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest problem (and my wife's, to an even greater degree) with that version was the fact that your Seeming came down to a single choice. Someone who lived a peaceful life, had a comparatively peaceful Durance, and tries to live a peaceful life afterwards is just as much an Ogre as someone who used violence for everything before, during, and after their Durance, provided that the first used violence that one time to escape. I'm not saying that having one decision forever shape a character is necessarily a bad thing (and I will still frequently make use of the option), but I like that the new version seems to place the greatest defining event into the players' hands rather than specifying what that defining event had to be. This change means that I can more easily convert characters from first edition to second without needing to decide between changing backstory or changing Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your escape is only a single moment and has no further effect on your life afterwords, I would have a hard time swallowing that moment as an act of reclaiming agency. A nonviolent person gets abducted, abused, disfigured, and eventually pushed to the point that they feel their only recourse is to fight their way out? That's not something that happens to a person and then they just move on with their lives like it never happened. That affects you. Even if the way it affects you is by making you regret the decision to go against your morals, and trying to atone for that act of violence by embracing absolute pacifism. The thing is, taking back your life from an abuser is never just &quot;one single choice.&quot; It is a life-changing event.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135201#post1135201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if my post seems antagonistic. It isn't intended to, but replying on my phone makes it a bit of a pain to keep going back to refine it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I too apologize if I'm coming off as aggressively defending the previous version of Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:07:36-07:00","id":1135232,"title":"","content":"So, I didn't went thru all the 4 pages of thread before this, but I thought OPP didn't kickstarted CofD corebooks (in fact the practice seemed to be destined exclusively for Scion, WoD20 and Exalted). Any clue why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:10:54-07:00","id":1135234,"title":"","content":"Willow's making all my points far more eloquently than I could on a phone and a 40 hour work week. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-29-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:12:26-07:00","id":1135235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135232#post1135232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I didn't went thru all the 4 pages of thread before this, but I thought OPP didn't kickstarted CofD corebooks (in fact the practice seemed to be destined exclusively for Scion, WoD20 and Exalted). Any clue why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Happened with new lines. Mummy, Demon and Beast had their Kickstarter. None of the &quot;old&quot; gamelines 2nd Edition core did, but Changeling indeed will. My humble guess? Popular demand. It's not one of the Big Three, but Changeling belongs to cool kids club when it comes to CofD<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's not a vitriolic remark, just me saying people love Changeling and the line is a really popular one. It's well earned success","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-29-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:16:35-07:00","id":1135237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135235#post1135235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happened with new lines. Mummy, Demon and Beast had their Kickstarter. None of the &quot;old&quot; gamelines 2nd Edition core did, but Changeling indeed will. My humble guess? Popular demand. It's not one of the Big Three, but Changeling belongs to cool kids club when it comes to CofD<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's not a vitriolic remark, just me saying people love Changeling and the line is a really popular one. It's well earned success</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like they want more fan oversight than other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:22:41-07:00","id":1135240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135237#post1135237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds more like they want more fan oversight than other games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am pretty sure it is just that they have decided it is worth doing Kickstarters now. The previous second edition books were mostly still started in the haze of the God-Machine update, and they now have the successful formula from the other CofD Kickstaters (Mummy, Demon, Beast, Dark Eras) to work from.<br /> <br /> The Open Dev process has been in place for the others as well, to whatever extant the Developer wanted it to be, that isn't changing now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:23:48-07:00","id":1135241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135237#post1135237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds more like they want more fan oversight than other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a factor, now that you mention it. A way to engage with the fan a bit more in order to show what the game is, which does make sense considering the change of developers and direction might cause some confusion to people about stylistical choices. It has the added benefit of allowing people to have a look and decide if they like what they see before buying.<br /> <br /> Can't really speak about the differences between versions myself. I tend to stay away from development in general because it's my weird way to deal with hype, but I still think the biggest reason is popular demand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T16:10:40-07:00","id":1135288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135111#post1135111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's made on much less way than in David's 2E Seemings, and his version narrative enforcement. Let's look on other 2E X-Splats, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire Clans</b> - beside nice fluff, most identity of them are only in Clan Bane, really - I can make 4 different Nosferatu vampires on the rules, not going against splat write-up in 2E corebook, it's so ambiguous. They<i> literally</i> give you three different origins stories of each Clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf Auspices</b> - It's only tells you 'what way you hunt' - just like Seeming tells you 'what way you are fae' in 1E. Adding Moon Phases is nice tie-in, but not really limiting character concepts - any one can be made to First Change on 'First Quarter of the Moon'.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage Paths</b> - Two Ruling Arcana and Supernal Beings you summon or see in Mage Sight. All that it is here, really. Added Tarot assosiation is nice fluff, but not really limiting players choices in character creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Linages</b> - The way you were Created plus your Humor. Maybe a bit more enforcing than rest, but it's only limited to how Demiurge or Genitor took bodies that made you. From then on it's totally your story. It's on the same par as Kith, I may add.<br /> <br /> <b>David's 2E Changeling Seemings</b> - All of them assume you won you freedom from Keeper cretin way - you needed to do things that define each David's Seemings, nothing other will grant you powers, Curse and Blessing of Seeming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It works great if you agree with David's Seeming vision - but it alienates anyone other not agreeing with his 'Seemings stories'. I like to play sometimes 'rebel leading Faeirest' - but also 'immoral princess', making her much more Gentry-like.<br /> <br /> I will be direct here - to point out that David's Seemings are extremely restricting the players' background in comparison to the other 2E games. That's why open definition of Rose's is really way to go with it - if you agree with David's vision, you totally still can have it. If you not - you all are still fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it hilarious your arguement is &quot;X has too restricting flavour because it's more restricting than Y and Z .... after I tore viciously away all of the flavour from Y and Z&quot;. Also, Path really matters to the fluff of mage considering it determines how your gnosis works, how your character sees reality through their abilities, their signature, and their yantra selection. It amazes me someone could try to treat it as if it did nothing but just &quot;I'm good at x magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;you need to do specific things and nothing other will grant you powers&quot; is very misleading. It's &quot;If how you're breaking free of your keeper is actually interesting, you get a seeming which reflects how you took back your agency&quot;. You don't get a seeming if your story of agency is just &quot;Oh, the door was open and no one even bothered to try and stop you&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-29-2017, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T16:41:55-07:00","id":1135294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135288#post1135288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it hilarious your arguement is &quot;X has too restricting flavour because it's more restricting than Y and Z .... after I tore viciously away all of the flavour from Y and Z&quot;. Also, Path really matters to the fluff of mage considering it determines how your gnosis works, how your character sees reality through their abilities, their signature, and their yantra selection. It amazes me someone could try to treat it as if it did nothing but just &quot;I'm good at x magic&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because what path you choose <b><u>can be</u></b> (not is, can be) irrelevant to your background. You might care about how your character seer reality through magic etc etc. Others can just ignore it and do it because of their personal character concept and ignore all the flavor of the author. Kinda difficult to do it on Seeming as it was written. Unlike Hill\u00b4s seeming there isnt a &quot;you must do this X way to awaken in this or that way&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not everyone cares about clan or Paths beyond the mechanics. They got a character concept that requires said clan or path and thats that. The game rarely should intervene with player taste in such arbitrary way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135288#post1135288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;you need to do specific things and nothing other will grant you powers&quot; is very misleading. It's &quot;If how you're breaking free of your keeper is actually interesting, you get a seeming which reflects how you took back your agency&quot;. You don't get a seeming if your story of agency is just &quot;Oh, the door was open and no one even bothered to try and stop you&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are assuming that everyones finds the act of escaping as compelling as you do and that in sets you on a specific seeming as something universally good. Which isnt.<br /> <br /> As other, including myself, have pointed out the issue is that the people who have complain about seeming are those that have a disonance between Hills narrow vision of &quot;this 5 ways to escape that correlate to this 5 seemings&quot;. In which they have a character concept that by either background and prefference is tied to the wrong Seeming for what they player wants and in the end if i have to choose for something that not all player are gonna find relevant. Some player do wanna put lot of though on their escape while other just wanna play urban fantasy in WoD and all the in-between of player latching on other themes of changeling and leaving the escape as a afterthough or part of a history outside of Hills purview.<br /> <br /> Say a players wants to play a fairest that was just discarded as a broken toy by her Fae and had to find her way back. Perfectly valid concept except under Hills invasive seeming mechanic.<br /> <br /> Also while seeming is a contested issue there are many other things we dont really know how they gonna end up in 2nd. I think the only sureties are Contracts, Courts** and pledge system. Still has to be seen if things like the convoluted mess of plot convinience that were fae touched and the invasive concept of Huntsmen are still gonna make it on the final version.<br /> <br /> **They still doing the whole &quot;they gain a contract of *insert emotion&quot;, a contract of &quot;*insert element* and a talespinning contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-29-2017, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:10:30-07:00","id":1135297,"title":"","content":"I think that part of the reason that some people had a problem with the Underhill Seemings is that they still look at the Seemings like they were in first edition. In first edition, Seeming was something done to you, with Kith as a further refinement of that idea. Underhill made that the purview of Kith alone, and Seeming became the manner of your escape. That meant that for some people, their beloved character suddenly would be something completely different. The Render Ogre that secretly tunneled his way to freedom would now be something else entirely (Beast, maybe, since most people don't spend their spare moments building a secret tunnel? Wizened, perhaps, if he truly mastered the art of mining and replaced his stone claws with the edge of a pick?). For the player to still have that character as an Ogre, there'd need to be someone that they hurt on the way out. I think the problem there is less &quot;I want my character to have escaped by violence without resorting to violence,&quot; and more of &quot;I don't want my Ogre character to now be a Beast, but I also don't want to change the backstory.&quot; Perhaps I'm forgetting, but did the edition change for any of the other games result in characters that would belong to an entirely different splat without a change in backstory? Rose's version seems to offer both &quot;You can make your Seeming about your escape&quot; and &quot;You can keep playing your existing character without needing to change the backstory,&quot; which I like because I plan to mix and match. To me, it seems more personal that you can choose how you came to have your Seeming, rather than it being just, &quot;You stabbed a guy on the way out? Okay, you're an Ogre. Unless he was your buddy, then Darkling is also an option.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:30:39-07:00","id":1135299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because what path you choose <b><u>can be</u></b> (not is, can be) irrelevant to your background. You might care about how your character seer reality through magic etc etc. Others can just ignore it and do it because of their personal character concept and ignore all the flavor of the author. Kinda difficult to do it on Seeming as it was written. Unlike Hill\u00b4s seeming there isnt a &quot;you must do this X way to awaken in this or that way&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not everyone cares about clan or Paths beyond the mechanics. They got a character concept that requires said clan or path and thats that. The game rarely should intervene with player taste in such arbitrary way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't care about Seeming beyond mechanics, why should the writers care what your opinion of the fluff is? You're just going to ignore it anyway, might as well make sure it's good for the people who do care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are assuming that everyones finds the act of escaping as compelling as you do and that in sets you on a specific seeming as something universally good. Which isnt.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're well aware that not everyone finds it compelling. Not everyone finds the Pilgrimage compelling either, but Promethean is a better game for focusing on it. I'd rather the games focus on being the best they can be for the people they appeal to than water themselves down for the sake of a broader appeal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As other, including myself, have pointed out the issue is that the people who have complain about seeming are those that have a disonance between Hills narrow vision of &quot;this 5 ways to escape that correlate to this 5 seemings&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we stop with this reductionist presentation? There are far more than 5 ways to escape that fit in with the 5 Seemings. Give me a means of escape that is also a means of reclaiming agency and I can tell you which Seeming it fits into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which they have a character concept that by either background and prefference is tied to the wrong Seeming for what they player wants and in the end if i have to choose for something that not all player are gonna find relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Underhill Seemings are defined by the means of escape. What is it about the seeming that the character prefers so much? When Darkling is defined as &quot;people who used pragmatic means of escape,&quot; why is it so important to you that your character who didn't escape through pragmatic means be a Darkling? I can't help but feel like this dissonance springs from a refusal to meet that take on Seemings on its own terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some player do wanna put lot of though on their escape while other just wanna play urban fantasy in WoD and all the in-between of player latching on other themes of changeling and leaving the escape as a afterthough or part of a history outside of Hills purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then those players can just pick a Seeming they think is cool and leave the background vague. Or stick with the typical example - that's <i>exactly what the examples are there for.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a players wants to play a fairest that was just discarded as a broken toy by her Fae and had to find her way back. Perfectly valid concept except under Hills invasive seeming mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that the definition of Fairest under David's version of Seemings is someone who escaped by taking charge. A character who was just discarded as a broken toy is by definition not a Fairest under that take on Seeming. What does being a Fairest do for that character concept that makes it so important?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also while seeming is a contested issue there are many other things we dont really know how they gonna end up in 2nd. I think the only sureties are Contracts, Courts** and pledge system. Still has to be seen if things like the convoluted mess of plot convinience that were fae touched and the invasive concept of Huntsmen are still gonna make it on the final version.<br /> <br /> **They still doing the whole &quot;they gain a contract of *insert emotion&quot;, a contract of &quot;*insert element* and a talespinning contract?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, I Really can't find a polite way to respond to this. Would it kill you to be a little less deriding about game elements you personally dislike?<br /> <br /> At any rate, I've accepted that David's version of Seemings won't be making it into 2e. At this point, it's the Clarity mechanics that I really care about (though, those do tie into the Seeming mechanics. I'm holding out hope that if they do preserve Clarity, they'll find a way to make the new take on Seemings work passably with it). That's the deciding factor for me. I already said my piece on that, now I'm just here defending Underhill changeling from unfair accusations of rigidity based on uncharitably rigid readings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:37:28-07:00","id":1135302,"title":"","content":"One weird thing to me is the idea that &quot;I can't be like an ogre in appearance without the ogre seeming despite the fact that kith still can give you an ogre appearance&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135294#post1135294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because what path you choose <b><u>can be</u></b> (not is, can be) irrelevant to your background. You might care about how your character seer reality through magic etc etc. Others can just ignore it and do it because of their personal character concept and ignore all the flavor of the author. Kinda difficult to do it on Seeming as it was written. Unlike Hill\u00b4s seeming there isnt a &quot;you must do this X way to awaken in this or that way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your ignoring all the flavour.... then Seeming's flavour shouldn't be a problem... You're being really hypocritical. As I said before, &quot;X has too restricting flavour because it's more restricting than Y and Z .... after I tore viciously away all of the flavour from Y and Z&quot; is a pretty ridiculous argument. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everyone cares about clan or Paths beyond the mechanics. They got a character concept that requires said clan or path and thats that. The game rarely should intervene with player taste in such arbitrary way. </div> </div> </div>Then play with seemings in the same way? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are assuming that everyones finds the act of escaping as compelling as you do and that in sets you on a specific seeming as something universally good. Which isnt. </div> </div> </div>Not really.... I just want them to pick Something for seeming to represent, rather than it potentially representing nearly anything. Every gameline has it's mechanics tie into the narrative to reinforce the themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As other, including myself, have pointed out the issue is that the people who have complain about seeming are those that have a disonance between Hills narrow vision of &quot;this 5 ways to escape that correlate to this 5 seemings&quot;. In which they have a character concept that by either background and prefference is tied to the wrong Seeming for what they player wants and in the end if i have to choose for something that not all player are gonna find relevant. Some player do wanna put lot of though on their escape while other just wanna play urban fantasy in WoD and all the in-between of player latching on other themes of changeling and leaving the escape as a afterthough or part of a history outside of Hills purview. </div> </div> </div>It's not Hills narrow vision... it's yours. You're the one acting as though there are only six available durance stories. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say a players wants to play a fairest that was just discarded as a broken toy by her Fae and had to find her way back. Perfectly valid concept except under Hills invasive seeming mechanic. </div> </div> </div>What is wrong with that character concept being one of the seemingless? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still has to be seen if things like the convoluted mess of plot convinience that were fae touched and the invasive concept of Huntsmen are still gonna make it on the final version. </div> </div> </div>We get it, you disliked hills version. -.-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-29-2017, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:45:12-07:00","id":1135303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135297#post1135297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I'm forgetting, but did the edition change for any of the other games result in characters that would belong to an entirely different splat without a change in backstory?</div> </div> </div> </div>No that i know of. Clans are pretty much the same in 2nd, same as paths. Maybe there was a difference in 1st edition in the limitations of summoning for mages. <br /> <br /> And maybe on auspices, some rituals in Forsaken were made into lunar powers for specific auspice so if you wanted a Rahu (full moon uratha) who made oaths then you would have to find a DM who allows you to port (easy to do) the 1st ritual or change auspice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135297#post1135297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose's version seems to offer both &quot;You can make your Seeming about your escape&quot; and &quot;You can keep playing your existing character without needing to change the backstory,&quot; which I like because I plan to mix and match. To me, it seems more personal that you can choose how you came to have your Seeming, rather than it being just, &quot;You stabbed a guy on the way out? Okay, you're an Ogre. Unless he was your buddy, then Darkling is also an option.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Also there is to see if the 2nd edition would do with Seeming curses which are raw. Is one of those &quot;good in theory but bad when you thing about it&quot; issues. As we are discussing seemings i check the back again and wow, some are problematic.<br /> <br /> Example: Wizened loose a point of clarity when they fail (not dramatic fail) a roll related to their talent.....which is doesnt seem that bad (because we assume that a character is gonna put point in said skill) but honestly Chrod system is so wonky that i see a PC falling more rolls on his talent than he gains clarity as he can only regain clarity from a successful action once.<br /> <br /> Darkling blessing is that they regain a clarity point (not upper limit for this) when he makes a makes a wrong choice for another character or take the hard choice then he regains. Which i am seeing it turning into the malkavian fishmalk problem of old Vampire. &quot;Why we will be with a character whose agenda is disruptive to ours?&quot;<br /> <br /> Darkling curse is trusting blindly in someone which is....weird? A PC can just declare he &quot;distrusful&quot; and nothing will happen. <br /> <br /> Fairest curse makes playing a general (either summer or West court) almost impossible as if one of their troops get gravely injured then they loose clarity. Which would have made more sense for it to be &quot;when their order proves to be the wrong one&quot;.<br /> <br /> Beast blessing is to harsh as one can only regain it by suffering personal cost (which is something not asked by other blessings). <br /> <br /> They are in the end pretty raw as mechanic goes. All of them are just tied to clarity, except the Wizened for some reason. I mean is a minor complain as i can just port the 1st edition blessing and curses but still. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:45:39-07:00","id":1135304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135297#post1135297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that part of the reason that some people had a problem with the Underhill Seemings is that they still look at the Seemings like they were in first edition. In first edition, Seeming was something done to you, with Kith as a further refinement of that idea. Underhill made that the purview of Kith alone, and Seeming became the manner of your escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is absolutely the root of the problem. That's what I was getting at in my previous post about people refusing to meet David's presentation of Seemings on its own terms. Personally, I think it was a much better choice to make &quot;what was done to you&quot; entirely under the purview of Kith, because 1e Kith and Seeming took 1e Werewolf's &quot;Tribe is just a second Auspice&quot; problem to an even greater extreme. I'd rather Kith and Seeming have distinct meanings in the meta-narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135297#post1135297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That meant that for some people, their beloved character suddenly would be something completely different. The Render Ogre that secretly tunneled his way to freedom would now be something else entirely (Beast, maybe, since most people don't spend their spare moments building a secret tunnel? Wizened, perhaps, if he truly mastered the art of mining and replaced his stone claws with the edge of a pick?). For the player to still have that character as an Ogre, there'd need to be someone that they hurt on the way out. I think the problem there is less &quot;I want my character to have escaped by violence without resorting to violence,&quot; and more of &quot;I don't want my Ogre character to now be a Beast, but I also don't want to change the backstory.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, what &quot;being an Ogre&quot; represented changed. If your character didn't escape by violence, there's really no reason to cling to that character having been an Ogre. That could all be represented by your character's Kith, which freed you up to pick a Seeming that was more meaningful to your character's story than &quot;the Seeming the Kith I wanted was attached to.&quot; Changing your 1e Ogre to a 2e Beast wouldn't have meant anything about the character would have had to change, so why the attachment to that Seeming? Just the name &quot;Ogre&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135297#post1135297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I'm forgetting, but did the edition change for any of the other games result in characters that would belong to an entirely different splat without a change in backstory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Promethean. Since Unfleshed became a Lineage, lots of characters who had been other Lineages in 1e would have changed to Unfleshed unless their backstory was tweaked a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135297#post1135297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose's version seems to offer both &quot;You can make your Seeming about your escape&quot; and &quot;You can keep playing your existing character without needing to change the backstory,&quot; which I like because I plan to mix and match. To me, it seems more personal that you can choose how you came to have your Seeming, rather than it being just, &quot;You stabbed a guy on the way out? Okay, you're an Ogre. Unless he was your buddy, then Darkling is also an option.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, if means of escape isn't always what defines one's Seeming, then Seeming no longer represents a reclamation of agency. Even if you claim &quot;it can represent that if you want it to&quot;, that makes the metaphor significantly less poignant. It makes Seeming's narrative role less specific and more nebulous. I've accepted that the agency metaphor isn't sticking around, I just wish they would make a strong choice with what's going to replace it instead of waffling. I'd rather Changeling focus on telling its story well than try to be everything to everyone at the cost of narrative focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-29-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:57:30-07:00","id":1135306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135303#post1135303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there is to see if the 2nd edition would do with Seeming curses which are raw. Is one of those &quot;good in theory but bad when you thing about it&quot; issues. As we are discussing seemings i check the back again and wow, some are problematic.<br /> <br /> Example: Wizened loose a point of clarity when they fail (not dramatic fail) a roll related to their talent.....which is doesnt seem that bad (because we assume that a character is gonna put point in said skill) but honestly Chrod system is so wonky that i see a PC falling more rolls on his talent than he gains clarity as he can only regain clarity from a successful action once.<br /> <br /> Darkling blessing is that they regain a clarity point (not upper limit for this) when he makes a makes a wrong choice for another character or take the hard choice then he regains. Which i am seeing it turning into the malkavian fishmalk problem of old Vampire. &quot;Why we will be with a character whose agenda is disruptive to ours?&quot;<br /> <br /> Darkling curse is trusting blindly in someone which is....weird? A PC can just declare he &quot;distrusful&quot; and nothing will happen.<br /> <br /> Fairest curse makes playing a general (either summer or West court) almost impossible as if one of their troops get gravely injured then they loose clarity. Which would have made more sense for it to be &quot;when their order proves to be the wrong one&quot;.<br /> <br /> Beast blessing is to harsh as one can only regain it by suffering personal cost (which is something not asked by other blessings).<br /> <br /> They are in the end pretty raw as mechanic goes. All of them are just tied to clarity, except the Wizened for some reason. I mean is a minor complain as i can just port the 1st edition blessing and curses but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are making the mistake of assuming that a Breaking Point means Clarity loss. Remember, in Underhill Changeling, Breaking Points are the only way to regain Clarity outside of the Seeming Blessing.<br /> <br /> The main thing Seeming did for you in Underhill Changeling was give you a free point of Clarity once per story when you commit an act that recalls the means by which you reclaimed your agency, and gives you an extra Breaking Point related to the trauma you experienced in your Durance, which effectively a high-risk-high reward way of maintaining Clarity. It also provided a few examples of how your appearance might vary from others of your Kith, and a few free 1-exp bonuses on certain Contracts. That's why it's so weird to me that opponents of this take on Seeming are so attached to the idea of characters being certain Seemings despite their means of escape not lining up with those Seemings. Your Seeming is defined pretty much entirely by your means of escape, not just narratively but mechanically as well. So why is it so important that your pacifist character be an Ogre? There's nothing about the Blessing or Curse that would tie in with that character's backstory, nothing about the Blessing or Curse that would benefit the character, and that's 90% of what Ogre is under this system. Do you really want that one Ogre Contract bonus so badly? It only costs you 1 exp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T18:11:11-07:00","id":1135307,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned before, I tend to avoid development threads, but I had the idea that pretty much everyone liked the Huntsmen (which I admit knowing about only through echo chamber, for the aforementioned reasons).<br /> <br /> Is there much difference between David's and Rose's take on them? Because I swear this is the first time I see people complaining about them and, for the little I heard about them in recent threads, they seem quite awesome.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if I drop in knowing little. I was more of an absent lurker when David was at the lead and what I read about 2nd Edition can be reduced pretty much to the latest discussions and mentions Rose made, which I do like overall)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-29-2017, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T18:19:36-07:00","id":1135309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135307#post1135307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned before, I tend to avoid development threads, but I had the idea that pretty much everyone liked the Huntsmen (which I admit knowing about only through echo chamber, for the aforementioned reasons).<br /> <br /> Is there much difference between David's and Rose's take on them? Because I swear this is the first time I hard people complaining about them and, for the little I heard about them in recent threads, they seem quite awesome.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if I drop in knowing little. I was more of an absent lurker when David was at the lead and what I read about 2nd Edition can be reduced pretty much to the latest discussions and mentions Rose made, which I do like overall)</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. Frankly this is a welcome change of topic.<br /> <br /> Unless I missed something, we don't really know much about Huntsmen in Rose's version. They will probably be at least a little different than David's Huntsmen though, because David's Huntsmen relies heavily on a resource called Yearning, which was closely tied with his Court and Bulwark mechanics, and we know Courts are changing a fair bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T18:39:05-07:00","id":1135310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135299#post1135299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're well aware that not everyone finds it compelling. Not everyone finds the Pilgrimage compelling either, but Promethean is a better game for focusing on it. I'd rather the games focus on being the best they can be for the people they appeal to than water themselves down for the sake of a broader appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the thing. The pilgrimage is not the same as the escape. One is, i think, a process, the other is a moment inside a larger process. I dont know the exacts of promethean so i am gonna compare it to mage, its like saying &quot;not everyone find the choice pen in which you wrote your name on the watchtower compelling&quot; and i am not saying that dismissively there was a interesting imagery of a, i think thyrsus, mage having to choose carefully the tools to write his name but even then that just one part of the awakening and there is a whole lot of before and after during the whole process. Same with the Durance, some find the escape compelling, other find the enduring compelling and other finds the reaching the human world compelling but all of that in part of the large process of the &quot;durance&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135299#post1135299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we stop with this reductionist presentation? There are far more than 5 ways to escape that fit in with the 5 Seemings. Give me a means of escape that is also a means of reclaiming agency and I can tell you which Seeming it fits into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay i have to quote yourself here because even you said it yourself<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1134731#post1134731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is a shallow reading. All fairest escape through <i>taking charge</i>, not necessarily through leadership, though leadership is a good example of one way this might be expressed. All Ogres escaped through violence, yes. All Wizened escaped through mastery of... something.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135299#post1135299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, Underhill Seemings are defined by the means of escape. What is it about the seeming that the character prefers so much? When Darkling is defined as &quot;people who used pragmatic means of escape,&quot; why is it so important to you that your character who didn't escape through pragmatic means be a Darkling? I can't help but feel like this dissonance springs from a refusal to meet that take on Seemings on its own terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is more of a refusal to take the, in that moment, new take on seeming on its own term because one find its limiting. Maybe the player likes the fluff of the Seeming but his character concept requires a different kind of escape. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> put it better on his post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135299#post1135299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then those players can just pick a Seeming they think is cool and leave the background vague. Or stick with the typical example - that's <i>exactly what the examples are there for.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Doesnt it also affect the ways your character looks? Because nothing on what i read on say for example on Ogres says that i can make a legolas-like elf<br /> <br /> &quot;To the Changeling, the Ogre takes up more space than it seems like she should. The floor slopes toward her as if the weight of her potential violence in inevitable, a slow slide. Joists in the ceiling bend to make room for her head, if she\u2019s actually that tall or not. She\u2019s not got skin, or if she does, it\u2019s softness is hidden behind a layer of something harder. It might be patchy, or a complete shell, but by and large, any visible part of the Ogre is hidden behind tough leather, stone, mud, scales, anything but delicate human skin.&quot;<br /> <br /> But on the same note, can you make YOUR changeling seeming defining moment be the moment of escape and let the other player choose theirs in their games?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135299#post1135299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the definition of Fairest under David's version of Seemings is someone who escaped by taking charge. A character who was just discarded as a broken toy is by definition not a Fairest under that take on Seeming. What does being a Fairest do for that character concept that makes it so important?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again thats that game restricting the player in where it shouldnt. Maybe he likes that escape for his changeling but like to RP the blessing and curse of the fairest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135299#post1135299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, I Really can't find a polite way to respond to this. Would it kill you to be a little less deriding about game elements you personally dislike?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay lets be fair here, what i says is pretty much fact.<br /> <br /> Fae touched in 1st edition: The changeling equivalent of a half baked cookie, you escape before the changes were made all the way through. You stuck in the in-between.<br /> Fae touched in 2nd edition: A human who happens to have made a meaningful promise to another mortal who was taken, the the former mortal has to decide to follow a trail into the hedge (and the chageling has to be alive at that moment though that isnt very clear), he has to happen to survive it and return (with changeling or not).<br /> <br /> Thats a lot of stars in the right place at the same time. So you need to 2 humans who make a meaningful promise to each other. One to be taken and survive until the other steps on the hedge and the latter to survive the trip. There is plenty of criticism to 1st edition Fae touched, most glaring was how they were pointless but one thing you cannot say with a straight face is that the 1st wasnt more straightforward than the second edition one.<br /> <br /> On huntsmen. I have mixed feeling about new antagonist of the 2nd edition lines so far (Strix and Idigam) from critiques on how much space it was dedicate to what it can only be a &quot;big bad of the season&quot; instead of more regular antagonist that would see more use in werewolf and &quot;good idea bad execution&quot; with vampire. None of them was as invasive as the huntmen, you got the feeling you could ignore the Idigam and the strix and little would change. Not the same with the Huntsmen, the whole court system exist just to keep them at bay, a big chunk of the society was dedicated to the (i think it was name tokens the &quot;you dont chase me anymore&quot; objects) dealings of them. They are integral part of Hills version of changeling in a way that neither the Strix or Idigam were. Like most consideration of power and enemies have take into account the Huntsmen. Instead of being yet another antagonist that one can throw at the PCs, they feel like THE inescapable antagonist to throw at them. You might like it or hate it but they are invasive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T18:59:45-07:00","id":1135314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135307#post1135307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there much difference between David's and Rose's take on them? Because I swear this is the first time I see people complaining about them and, for the little I heard about them in recent threads, they seem quite awesome.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if I drop in knowing little. I was more of an absent lurker when David was at the lead and what I read about 2nd Edition can be reduced pretty much to the latest discussions and mentions Rose made, which I do like overall)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well from what I can gather:<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, the open dev material revealed by Rose and Meghan shown that has any counterpart to David's open dev material is completely different from his. So much so that out of the material released, none David's material has seemingly carried over. This includes:<br /> <br /> -The Hedge write-up: just in general the portrayal of the Hedge being different from David's by not focusing as much on &quot;Hedge = PAIN!&quot; but on more of it being an actual place.<br /> -The sample city settings: Toronto and Honshu were previewed for David's CtL2e, but in Rose and Meghan's version we have instead New Orleans. And it does look like David's city settings aren't being carried over.<br /> -The Autumn Court: in how it references changes to Courts due to certain aspects of David's Courts are not present (such as the Bulwark trait)<br /> -Seemings: (aka the one being contested right now) first hinted at being changed in the True Fae open dev blog.<br /> <br /> Thus far the stuff that I've seen here that people seem to be reasonably ok with in Rose's and Meghan's CtL2e are:<br /> <br /> -The Tumbledown Market/New Orleans write up<br /> -Contracts (General and Seeming Contracts are gone and now rolled together as Arcadian Contracts, and the Seeming side of it has been remade into a sub-category called Regalia. David's Contracts, amusingly, more closely resembled 1e's Contracts then Rose's and Meghan's version)<br /> -Goblin Debt (new mechanic tied to Goblin Contracts)<br /> -True Fae<br /> -Storytelling chapter<br /> <br /> (and everyone just seems to mutually be &quot;meh&quot; at the Merits preview, but then again, Merits)<br /> <br /> If I left anything out or put something that's not true, feel free to correct me.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Me personally: I suspect that because David left OPP, his material being altered or unusable.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I'm not entirely familiar with OPP's policies regarding this kind of thing, but I would guess that publishing material for a writer that is no longer tied to the company would present a bunch of legal issues. So they couldn't publish and sell David's CtL2e period.<br /> <br /> And I suspect they've been silent on what specifically has changed since...well...they're waiting on the KS so that they can just show everything at once instead of doing it bit by bit through forum or blog posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:11:57-07:00","id":1135317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135306#post1135306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are making the mistake of assuming that a Breaking Point means Clarity loss. Remember, in Underhill Changeling, Breaking Points are the only way to regain Clarity outside of the Seeming Blessing. The main thing Seeming did for you in Underhill Changeling was give you a free point of Clarity once per story when you commit an act that recalls the means by which you reclaimed your agency, and gives you an extra Breaking Point related to the trauma you experienced in your Durance, which effectively a high-risk-high reward way of maintaining Clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, i have the playtest compilation V6 and searched the PDFand i couldnt find how suffering a breaking point allows you to regain clarity. Even in an exceptional success you only gain:<br /> <br /> &quot;Extraordinary Success: Your character sees through the fogs that cloud her vision. She has a brief moment of revelation that grants her the Acuity Condition, and one other such as the Inspired Condition or similar Condition representing a newfound focus.&quot;<br /> <br /> so maybe that was posted in a forum post? Or somewhere else maybe? Not saying is not there just that it wasnt on the material i could find.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Charlaquin;n1135306] It also provided a few examples of how your appearance might vary from others of your Kith, and a few free 1-exp bonuses on certain Contracts. That's why it's so weird to me that opponents of this take on Seeming are so attached to the idea of characters being certain Seemings despite their means of escape not lining up with those Seemings. Your Seeming is defined pretty much entirely by your means of escape, not just narratively but mechanically as well.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the preview describes both background, appearance and imagery. If Seeming was &quot;just the moment you escape&quot; and some extra mechanics then it shouldn't, specially considering a 2nd of edition of a game, use the naming choice it used. Wizened, Fairest, Ogre, Darkling, elemental and beast invoke very specific imagery to ones mind with lots of preconceptions and the preview does little to dissuade them. If the wanted to make Seeming to not affect anything beyond the escape and clarity triggers then it wouldn't have been better to name them:<br /> <br /> Fairest &quot;Leader&quot;<br /> Darkling &quot;Pragmatic&quot;<br /> Ogre &quot;Aggresor&quot;<br /> Wizened &quot;Expert&quot;<br /> Elemental &quot;Survivor&quot;<br /> Beast &quot;Rebel&quot;<br /> <br /> No example of appearance, nor background or anything beyond that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135306#post1135306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So why is it so important that your pacifist character be an Ogre? There's nothing about the Blessing or Curse that would tie in with that character's backstory, nothing about the Blessing or Curse that would benefit the character, and that's 90% of what Ogre is under this system. Do you really want that one Ogre Contract bonus so badly? It only costs you 1 exp.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is many answers to that and it all depends on the player in question. Maybe the Blessing and curse dont tie in on the character backstory but it ties perfectly into the character ongoing struggle. There is also a narrative difference between being stuck with certain powers from you durance and buying them, the former implies intent with the former implies imposition and even a sense of being stuck with something illfitted (to the character no the player). There is a lot of interesting character concept and idea that are constrained by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-29-2017, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:19:08-07:00","id":1135320,"title":"","content":"Can we perhaps agree to disagree? While the level of discourse has been high and there have been some enlightening points of design made on both sides, edition wars can only last for so long before devolving and given the circumstances of why there is both a 2e and Underhill edition, I don't think we want to go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:30:59-07:00","id":1135322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135317#post1135317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, i have the playtest compilation V6 and searched the PDFand i couldnt find how suffering a breaking point allows you to regain clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loki, you very specifically didn't remember how Underhill Clarity worked. Remember those Conditions I mentioned? The one you get for succeeding on a breaking point roll lets you hit a story beat related to solidifying your place in your life to resolve the Condition and get a free dot of Clarity. That's what Acuity is, and the only other published source of that Condition was a once-per-story effect in the Fairest bonus for Read Lucidity. There was a whole discussion about how this recontextualized the Seeming previews back when the mechanics of Underhill Clarity were shared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:31:02-07:00","id":1135323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135307#post1135307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there much difference between David's and Rose's take on them? Because I swear this is the first time I see people complaining about them and, for the little I heard about them in recent threads, they seem quite awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on were you hang out. There were plenty of discussion about it on 4chan wod thread about it but at least for me there was no point on discussing it before on here. At least for me David Hills has a particular style and enforcement of his &quot;one true way&quot; of playing that i dislike, another freelancer was arcanearts on the project who shared his particular vision of changeling to a teeth so they seem like a umpenetrable blockade and just pointing out a complain would be answered with &quot;but we are aiming for a narrative......&quot; which is no different than &quot;we dont care what you think, if it doesnt fit our narrative&quot; so it seems like wasted effort to even put energy in a game that was a foregone conclusion.<br /> <br /> Month ago i just wrote changeling as a lost (lol) for me and was ready to ignore it and stick to first edition. But then well, a shitty situation happened but in the end a ray of hope (for me at least) shine throught. New developer, new ideas and a more &quot;do what you want&quot; feel to the game that it make me feel at least that there is room to discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:33:23-07:00","id":1135325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135322#post1135322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loki, you very specifically didn't remember how Underhill Clarity worked. Remember those Conditions I mentioned? The one you get for succeeding on a breaking point roll lets you hit a story beat related to solidifying your place in your life to resolve the Condition and get a free dot of Clarity. That's what Acuity is, and the only other published source of this Condition was a once-per-story effect in the Fairest bonus for Read Lucidity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh yes, you are right. Sorry i was focusing on checking the rolls results and effects of the condition result and didnt check the resolution as they normally are &quot;gain a beat&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:37:17-07:00","id":1135327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the thing. The pilgrimage is not the same as the escape. One is, i think, a process, the other is a moment inside a larger process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to go out on a limb here and guess that you've never been the victim of abuse? If I'm wrong I apologize, but this doesn't strike me as something most people who has been abused would say. Because escaping your abuser is never just a moment. Getting to the point where you're even willing to consider escape is a process. Building up the courage to attempt to escape is a process. Actually escaping is a process. And going on with your life after escaping is a lifelong process. Changeling the Lost is about the lattermost, and the former are all a part of what goes into Seeming. Granted, the escape itself is the most defining when it comes to Seeming in Underhill, but it is by no means a single moment in a larger process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know the exacts of promethean so i am gonna compare it to mage, its like saying &quot;not everyone find the choice pen in which you wrote your name on the watchtower compelling&quot; and i am not saying that dismissively there was a interesting imagery of a, i think thyrsus, mage having to choose carefully the tools to write his name but even then that just one part of the awakening and there is a whole lot of before and after during the whole process. Same with the Durance, some find the escape compelling, other find the enduring compelling and other finds the reaching the human world compelling but all of that in part of the large process of the &quot;durance&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those can and should play a part in your Seeming choice in Underhill. Seeming is not &quot;You punched a guy on your way out, so you're an Ogre, unless he was your friend, then you're a Darkling.&quot; It's not just a moment. Its the means by which you reclaimed agency. It's how you took your life back. It's the way you finally decided to put your foot down and say &quot;no more.&quot; Not an incidental thing that happened while you were running away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay i have to quote yourself here because even you said it yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>In that quote, I did not say there are only five ways of escaping, and if that's what you got out of that quote, then you are interpreting my words in a shallow manner as well as David's. There are countless ways one might flaunt social norms as a means of escape. There are countless ways one might make a pragmatic decision in order to escape. There are countless ways one might use their environment to escape. There are countless ways one might take charge in order to escape. There are countless ways one might use violence to escape. There are countless ways one might use their mastery of a skill to escape. If you have a specific story in mind that doesn't suit one of the above, you could always use one of the countless ways one might take control of the narrative their abuser has forced them into to escape. Or you could make a custom Seeming. Or you could go Unseemly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is more of a refusal to take the, in that moment, new take on seeming on its own term because one find its limiting. Maybe the player likes the fluff of the Seeming but his character concept requires a different kind of escape. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> put it better on his post.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff of the Seeming <i>is</i> the means of escape, so this hypothetical person is not meeting Underhill Seeming on its own terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesnt it also affect the ways your character looks? Because nothing on what i read on say for example on Ogres says that i can make a legolas-like elf<br /> <br /> &quot;To the Changeling, the Ogre takes up more space than it seems like she should. The floor slopes toward her as if the weight of her potential violence in inevitable, a slow slide. Joists in the ceiling bend to make room for her head, if she\u2019s actually that tall or not. She\u2019s not got skin, or if she does, it\u2019s softness is hidden behind a layer of something harder. It might be patchy, or a complete shell, but by and large, any visible part of the Ogre is hidden behind tough leather, stone, mud, scales, anything but delicate human skin.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the appearances are only examples. You can modify them to suit your needs. You could totally make a Legolas-like Ogre. Hell, that whole &quot;looks somehow bigger than they actually are&quot; thing is straight out of Tolkien. Galadriel does it when Frodo offers her the ring. Focus on elven Eminence for the size. Make the hardened skin be like flawless porcelain. These are all superficial details, easy to spin to suit one's needs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the same note, can you make YOUR changeling seeming defining moment be the moment of escape and let the other player choose theirs in their games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm going to have to, because we know Underhill Seeming is out. But as I've said before, the story is far less poignant when Seeming doesn't represent anything specific. I care more about the setting as a whole telling a compelling story than about my individual character having a compelling story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again thats that game restricting the player in where it shouldnt. Maybe he likes that escape for his changeling but like to RP the blessing and curse of the fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blessing and Curse of the Fairest relate <i>directly</i> to the Fairest's means of escape, so I don't understand this hypothetical desire to RP having one's sense of agency reinforced by taking the lead and being triggered by their leadership leading to collateral damage when the character's means of agency was kicking ass and taking names, or whatever else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay lets be fair here, what i says is pretty much fact.<br /> <br /> Fae touched in 1st edition: The changeling equivalent of a half baked cookie, you escape before the changes were made all the way through. You stuck in the in-between.<br /> Fae touched in 2nd edition: A human who happens to have made a meaningful promise to another mortal who was taken, the the former mortal has to decide to follow a trail into the hedge (and the chageling has to be alive at that moment though that isnt very clear), he has to happen to survive it and return (with changeling or not).<br /> <br /> Thats a lot of stars in the right place at the same time. So you need to 2 humans who make a meaningful promise to each other. One to be taken and survive until the other steps on the hedge and the latter to survive the trip. There is plenty of criticism to 1st edition Fae touched, most glaring was how they were pointless but one thing you cannot say with a straight face is that the 1st wasnt more straightforward than the second edition one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that it's all that contrived. In a setting where Faeries commonly take people from their lives, that some of those people would have close relationships with others, the sort that carry an implicit promise, whether of love, or care, or protection, or devotion, or partnership, or whatever else. Then to say that in this setting, such promises create a mystical bond that one can follow to find the stolen loved one, it makes sense that people sharing such bonds with Lost would often end up in the Hedge. Then, because of the nature of the Hedge (particularly in David's setting), if the loved one looses sight of their goal, they will likely end up wandering out again. It's also a very common fairy story, and a very powerful one. And there are less inflammatory ways to express an opinion that the story is contrived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135310#post1135310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On huntsmen. I have mixed feeling about new antagonist of the 2nd edition lines so far (Strix and Idigam) from critiques on how much space it was dedicate to what it can only be a &quot;big bad of the season&quot; instead of more regular antagonist that would see more use in werewolf and &quot;good idea bad execution&quot; with vampire. None of them was as invasive as the huntmen, you got the feeling you could ignore the Idigam and the strix and little would change. Not the same with the Huntsmen, the whole court system exist just to keep them at bay, a big chunk of the society was dedicated to the (i think it was name tokens the &quot;you dont chase me anymore&quot; objects) dealings of them. They are integral part of Hills version of changeling in a way that neither the Strix or Idigam were. Like most consideration of power and enemies have take into account the Huntsmen. Instead of being yet another antagonist that one can throw at the PCs, they feel like THE inescapable antagonist to throw at them. You might like it or hate it but they are invasive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. You could very easily leave Huntsmen out of your game. What Tokens and Bulwarks serve to do is insure that even if you do leave Huntsment out of your game, Changeling society is affected by the threat of Huntsmen. It gives the ST more options for how to generate conflict that don't directly involve throwing a Huntsmen at the PCs. And, you can still tell stories that don't involve any of the above if you want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-30-2017, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:51:23-07:00","id":1135332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135320#post1135320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we perhaps agree to disagree? While the level of discourse has been high and there have been some enlightening points of design made on both sides, edition wars can only last for so long before devolving and given the circumstances of why there is both a 2e and Underhill edition, I don't think we want to go there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be in support of that. As I've said before I'm resigned to the fact that the stuff I liked from David's Changeling isn't going to be in the official book (though if Clarity mechanics do end up being preserved it might get my interest back). I'm just responding to unfair accusations about David's Changeling in hopes of setting the record straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T20:36:50-07:00","id":1135337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135327#post1135327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go out on a limb here and guess that you've never been the victim of abuse? If I'm wrong I apologize, but this doesn't strike me as something most people who has been abused would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>...ok stop.<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume this wasn't your intention, but even then that bit really does sound like &quot;If you aren't an abuse survivor, you don't GET Changeling the Lost!&quot; Because now we're getting into some really sticky territory.<br /> <br /> Let's not go any further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T20:48:35-07:00","id":1135343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135337#post1135337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...ok stop.<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume this wasn't your intention, but even then that bit really does sound like &quot;If you aren't an abuse survivor, you don't GET Changeling the Lost!&quot; Because now we're getting into some really sticky territory.<br /> <br /> Let's not go any further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your assumption is correct, that was definitely not my intention. But you're right, that is iffy territory and I apologize for going there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:42:03-07:00","id":1135402,"title":"","content":"Why is a five-page derail still going on? Does a moderator being heavily involved absolve the thread from moderation?<br /> <br /> This topic of this thread wasn't 'How do you feel about the removal of David Hill's work'? There is literally more off-topic content in this thread than there is on-topic. I don't even know how to actually report something that's gotten this far out of hand.<br /> <br /> People are way too invested in arguing something that doesn't belong here, and as a result there are some really nasty implications being thrown around, too. What the hell guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:46:18-07:00","id":1135404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135402#post1135402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is a five-page derail still going on? Does a moderator being heavily involved absolve the thread from moderation?<br /> <br /> This topic of this thread wasn't 'How do you feel about the removal of David Hill's work'? There is literally more off-topic content in this thread than there is on-topic. I don't even know how to actually report something that's gotten this far out of hand.<br /> <br /> People are way too invested in arguing something that doesn't belong here, and as a result there are some really nasty implications being thrown around, too. What the hell guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, after 2 people in succession have decided to stop going off topic, how is complaining about being off topic helping?<br /> ___________<br /> Do we know roughly what month the Kickstarter will be and any of the stretch goals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:54:03-07:00","id":1135410,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135404#post1135404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, after 2 people in succession have decided to stop going off topic, how is complaining about being off topic helping?<br /> ___________</div> </div> </div> </div>More than two people were involved in the five-page derail. This post needs moderation, and the moderator involved is obviously too close to the issue to do it.<br /> <br /> To answer your question more specifically, it's helping because it gave me a non-mod post to actually flag so we can get moderation involved that isn't actually attached to this thread. It wasn't just to complain (although one might hope that having attention drawn to the extent of the derail might further convince the involved parties to knock it off)<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1135404#post1135404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDo we know roughly what month the Kickstarter will be and any of the stretch goals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of those pieces of info have been announced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:15:06-07:00","id":1135457,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything official/solid has been stated, but if I recall recorrectly, they mentioned at the panel (or on the forums somewhere, and I don't recall where) that late October/November is likely. <br /> <br /> So not too long (hopefully)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:04:08-07:00","id":1135470,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping October! the sooner the better for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Plus a Chronicles of Darkness Kickstarter that starts a bit before and goes through Halloween? Awesome Autumn Court timing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:27:32-07:00","id":1135482,"title":"","content":"Have there been any hints of OPP including backer-determined materials in any of their Kickstarters besides Dark Eras? It's presumably too late for this book (and maybe a bad idea for Core books in general) but it's something that would be cool to see more of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/a